
This project contains two types of datasets constructed for research on point cloud incompleteness, based on Spherical Removal and Axis Cut, each provided with 50% and 75% missing ratios.

1. Spherical Removal Dataset

Folder Names: data_ourh5(drop50), data_ourh5(drop75)

Generation Method: Randomly sample a spherical region within the overall point cloud and remove all points inside, simulating local incompleteness.

Missing Ratios:

    drop50: approximately 50% of points removed

    drop75: approximately 75% of points removed

File Structure:

    Completion3D_airplane/

       train/, val/, test/ subsets

    saveData_h5_convention/ and saveData_txt/ for intermediate or converted formats

    Associated .json files providing indexing and configuration

Characteristics: This method closely resembles missing data caused by local occlusions in real-world point cloud scanning.

2. Axis Cut Dataset

Folder Names: data_ourh5(axisCut50), data_ourh5(axisCut75)

Generation Method: Perform planar slicing along a coordinate axis and discard all points on one side of the slicing plane, simulating large-scale structural incompleteness.

Missing Ratios:

     axisCut50: approximately 50% of points removed

     axisCut75: approximately 75% of points removed

File Structure: Same as the spherical removal dataset (including train/, val/, test/ subsets and corresponding configuration files).

Characteristics: This method emphasizes extreme incompleteness scenarios, making it more suitable for testing model performance in large-scale missing and reconstruction tasks.
